<header class="ref-head yr-head"><p class="cty-kicker">Year by year · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p><h1 class="research-title">1955</h1><p class="ref-lede">1955 in world history: 29 events, 8 births, 19 deaths, 3 works, 1 state founded and 3 that came to an end. 360 recorded states existed that year.</p></header>
<nav class="ref-letters yr-near" aria-label="Nearby years"><a href="/years/1951">1951</a><a href="/years/1952">1952</a><a href="/years/1953">1953</a><a href="/years/1954">1954</a><a href="/years/1955" aria-current="page">1955</a><a href="/years/1956">1956</a><a href="/years/1957">1957</a><a href="/years/1958">1958</a><a href="/years/1959">1959</a></nav>
<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/anthony-eden" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/anthony-eden.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/april-5">5 April</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Winston Churchill resigns as Prime Minister</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Aged 80 and in failing health, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/winston-churchill">Winston Churchill</a> stepped down as Prime Minister and was succeeded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anthony-eden">Anthony Eden</a>. It closed a career at the top of British politics spanning more than half a century.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/united-kingdom">United Kingdom</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anthony-eden">Anthony Eden</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/april-12">12 April</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Salk's polio vaccine is declared safe and effective</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Results of a nationwide trial involving more than a million children showed Jonas Salk's vaccine worked. Mass vaccination soon cut polio cases dramatically.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/april-18">18 April</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Albert Einstein dies in Princeton</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albert-einstein">Albert Einstein</a> died aged 76. His theories of special and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theory-of-relativity">general relativity</a> and his work on light quanta transformed physics in the twentieth century.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/warsaw" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/warsaw.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/may-14">14 May</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Soviet bloc signs the Warsaw Pact</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The USSR and seven Eastern European states formed a military alliance days after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-germany">West Germany</a> joined <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nato">NATO</a>. The pact lasted until 1991.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warsaw">Warsaw</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/september-30">30 September</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">James Dean dies in a car crash aged 24</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Actor James Dean was killed when his Porsche collided with another car in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/california">California</a>. Two of his three starring films were released after his death, making him a lasting icon of youth.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/october-26">26 October</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Ngô Đình Diệm proclaims the Republic of Vietnam</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">After a heavily rigged referendum deposed the former emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bao-dai">Bảo Đại</a>, Ngô Đình Diệm proclaimed the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a> in the south. US support for the regime drew America into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam-war">Vietnam War</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/december-1">1 December</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Rosa Parks refuses to give up her bus seat</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rosa-parks">Rosa Parks</a> was arrested in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/montgomery-alabama">Montgomery, Alabama</a>, for refusing to give her seat to a white passenger. The 381-day bus boycott that followed brought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/martin-luther-king-jr">Martin Luther King Jr.</a> to national prominence.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/bandung-conference">Bandung Conference</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Asian–African Conference, or Bandung Conference, was a meeting of 29 newly independent and emerging states of Asia and Africa held at Bandung, Indonesia, in April 1955.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/austrian-state-treaty">Austrian State Treaty</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Austrian State Treaty, signed in Vienna on 15 May 1955 by the four occupying powers and Austria, restored Austria as a sovereign, independent and democratic state.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/philippeville-massacre">Philippeville massacre</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Philippeville massacre took place on 20 August 1955 in and around Philippeville, now Skikda, in north-eastern Algeria.</p></div></li></ol></section>
