0M12512 6227h0M12960 7182h0M12755 7128h0M19111 3007h0M18338 1857h0M13043 2547h0M11936 2066h0M12411 1613h0M12168 1689h0M12806 1120h0M12703 1200h0M12682 1268h0M12852 1984h0M13280 5526h0M12670 4873h0M12761 4972h0M12636 5052h0M12574 5201h0M12582 5313h0M12949 1347h0M12971 1242h0M13015 1059h0M12954 1083h0M12577 1419h0M12654 1408h0M12874 1192h0M11924 1823h0M18464 4874h0M19119 4624h0M18649 5527h0M6264 3376h0M6965 3761h0M7073 3840h0M7239 3762h0M7387 3898h0M7808 4236h0M8148 3441h0M7430 3075h0M7246 1660h0M7178 1510h0M6064 1862h0M1034 6767h0M1535 8233h0M19378 7831h0M13634 1222h0M14132 950h0M14132 950h0M13210 953h0M13406 760h0M13574 785h0M13831 749h0M13790 781h0M13650 893h0M13565 976h0M16906 2722h0M17212 2740h0M16310 2653h0M18391 3242h0M18602 4082h0M18481 4017h0M17783 3344h0M10973 4526h0M10701 3759h0M10678 4461h0"/></svg><figcaption><span class="map-key"><i class="k-p"></i>Profile</span><span class="map-key"><i class="k-s"></i>State</span><span>347 states with a known seat in 1955</span><a href="/atlas?year=1955">Open the atlas at 1955 &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure>
<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">In the profiles</h2><ul class="yr-prof"><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/indonesia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Indonesia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Indonesia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Indonesia hosts the Asian–African Conference at Bandung</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/anti-apartheid-movement"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Anti-apartheid%20movement.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Anti-apartheid movement</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Congress of the People adopts the Freedom Charter at Kliptown</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/government/chiefdom"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Chiefdom.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Chiefdom</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Kalervo Oberg names the chiefdom as a type; Elman Service sets it between tribe and state in 1962</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/federal-republic-of-germany"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Federal%20Republic%20of%20Germany.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Federal Republic of Germany</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">West Germany joins NATO; it is a founding member of the European Economic Community.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-austria"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Austria.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Austria</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Austrian State Treaty of 15 May restores full independence; on 26 October, with the occupation troops gone, parliament declares permanent neutrality.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/non-aligned-movement"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Non-Aligned%20Movement.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Non-Aligned Movement</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Bandung Conference of Asian and African states adopts a declaration that includes the Five Principles and a pledge of neutrality in the Cold War</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/peronism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Peronism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Peronism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Revolución Libertadora overthrows Perón, who goes into exile, and the Justicialist Party is banned</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-cambodia-1953-1970"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20Cambodia%20(1953-1970).png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of Cambodia (1953-1970)</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Sihanouk abdicates, founds the Sangkum and wins every seat in the National Assembly</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-vietnam"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Vietnam.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Vietnam</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Ngô Đình Diệm's referendum removes Bảo Đại as head of state, and on 26 October Diệm declares himself president of the Republic of Vietnam</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/jawaharlal-nehru"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Jawaharlal%20Nehru.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Jawaharlal Nehru</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">He is a key organiser of the Bandung Conference of newly independent nations from Asia and Africa</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/vienna"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Vienna.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Vienna</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Austrian State Treaty ends the four-power occupation</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/albert-einstein"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Albert%20Einstein.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Albert Einstein</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Dies at Princeton Hospital on 18 April, aged 76</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/martin-luther-king-jr"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Martin%20Luther%20King%20Jr..png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Martin Luther King Jr.</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Receives his PhD from Boston University and leads the Montgomery bus boycott, which lasts 385 days</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/sukarno"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Sukarno.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Sukarno</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">He hosts the Bandung Conference of Asian and African countries</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/juche"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Juche.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Juche</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Kim Il Sung gives the “Juche speech”, the first documented reference to Juche as an ideology</span></li></ul></section>
